General_Text_Description:
清　余奏言、顏炳　望雲山莊後圖八景　卷|Rear View of the Mountain Villa for Watching Clouds is a Qing dynasty (1644–1911) Handscroll by the China artist Yan Bing|Zhang Xianghe|Yu Zouyan. This piece, part of the Asian Art collection, is crafted using Handscroll; ink and color on paper. Measuring Frontispiece: 12 7/8 x 51 in (32.8 x 129.3 cm);
Painting by Yu Zouyan: 12 7/8 x 39 5/8 in (32.9 x 100.5 cm);
Poems by Zhang Xianghe: 12 1/4 x 74 1/2 in (31.1 x 189.2 cm);
Painting by Yan Bing: 12 3/8 x 78 1/2 in (31.3 x 199.5 cm, the work is classified as Paintings and was created in 1844–45.
